---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import RichContent from '../components/RichContent.astro';
import { sourcePages } from '../lib/content';
const team = sourcePages.find(page => page.slug === 'our-team')!;
---
<Layout title="Our story & people">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Get to know Abundant Earth" title="The future grows from connection." description="We believe the knowledge, care, and creativity to restore our world already exist in communities. Our work is to help those possibilities take root." />
  <section class="section container two-column"><div class="prose"><h2>A shared Earth.<br />A shared responsibility.</h2><p>Abundant Earth Foundation launched in 2018 to bring resources, skills, and people together in support of grassroots environmental and social restoration.</p><p>Our documented work connects permaculture, regenerative agriculture, and community-led initiatives with grants, strategic relationships, and practical assistance.</p><p>We support the people closest to local challenges: people growing food, teaching their neighbors, caring for ecosystems, and building more resilient ways of living.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">Meet the work <Icon /></a></div><figure><Photo name="seedlings" alt="Seedlings growing at Permaculture Paradise Institute, Malawi" class="wide-photo" /><figcaption>Permaculture Paradise Institute, Malawi · Photograph shared by ARC.</figcaption></figure></section>
  <section class="projects-section section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p><h2>Earth care. People care.<br /><em>Possibility for all.</em></h2><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><h3>Trust local knowledge.</h3><p>Community leaders understand their places. Support should strengthen their capacity to shape their own futures.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><h3>Connect the dots.</h3><p>Food security, healthy ecosystems, and livelihoods belong together. Regenerative approaches respond to those connections.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><h3>Share what helps.</h3><p>Small grants, teaching, mentorship, tools, and storytelling can each help good ideas move forward.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section container" id="team"><p class="eyebrow">People behind the connections</p><h2>A foundation built on relationships.</h2><p class="intro-description">The foundation’s published team page, updated May 4, 2026 and reviewed September 18, 2026, lists Hannah Eckberg and Alexa Bernard. Their source-published biographies are preserved below.</p><RichContent html={team.bodyHtml} /><p class="source-note"><a href={team.source}>View the source team page ↗</a></p></section>
  <section class="section container two-column" style="padding-top:0"><div class="prose"><h2>Built on trust.</h2><p>AEF is listed in public nonprofit records under EIN 36-4631367. Its archived donation page identifies the organization’s former name as Humboldt Plan It Green. That earlier organizational history explains why tax-exemption records begin before the 2018 AEF launch.</p><p>Clear records and honest reporting help supporters understand the work they make possible.</p><a class="text-link" href="/financials/">Financials & transparency <Icon /></a></div><div class="aside-card"><h3>Start a conversation.</h3><p>Have a question about the foundation, a possible collaboration, or an update to share?</p><a class="button button-outline" href="/contact/">Get in touch <Icon /></a></div></section>
  <section class="container section" style="padding-top:0"><a class="button button-outline" href="/how-we-help/">Our approach to grassroots philanthropy <Icon /></a><p class="source-note">Original identity from the foundation’s website:</p><img src="/images/legacy/1e8f4f44eeb7e321.webp" alt="Original Abundant Earth Foundation logo: restoring ecosystems" width="208" height="111" loading="lazy" /></section><CallToAction />
</Layout>
